From fbc1e9b9ca19e0b031f421fb3fd235361d8abd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(plugins): let plugins render the chat rows of their
 tools

A plugin can now list tool names (or prefixes ending in *) under
toolRenderers in its manifest and export renderTool(container, context,
host) from its module. Chat's ToolRenderer hands those rows to the plugin
with the tool input, result, status, theme, project and session, pushes
updates as the call streams and completes, and keeps the host rendering
whenever the plugin cannot draw. This lets an MCP-backed plugin present
its own tools, e.g. a delegated agent shown like a native subagent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
